WEBVTT

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.920
<i>Otome</i>:

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.840
A maiden, sweet-smelling as a flower,

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.930
a single bud blooming in a tranquil
garden, pure and dignified.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.230
Too shy to even speak of love or romance,

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:28.520
she dares not allow herself
to dream of a kiss.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:32.900
Even so, she blooms again today--

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.860
seeking, ever seeking
happiness beyond the stars.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:52.590
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:02.080
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:07.040
"Episode 5"
"September First"

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.840
What's the big idea, Tamako?

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:14.300
Suddenly you want to be a doctor?

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.050
And just <i>how</i>, exactly?

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:19.760
I telephoned Uncle Tamasuke.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:22.050
He said I could come by anytime.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:26.140
Uncle... Tamasuke?

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:28.730
Our uncle--he runs a clinic in Kobe.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:34.770
You know Father won't stand for it.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:37.570
A Shima daughter with
the title of "Doctor"?

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:40.280
You'll never find better bait.

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:43.030
I'll point that out; he'll be all for it.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:44.370
"Bait"?

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:47.450
Tamako-<i>san</i>...

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:55.420
Please, tell us how you're really feeling.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:59.170
You're Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>'s
precious sister, of course,

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:03.850
and now you're like a dear
little sister to me, too.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:06.930
That's why we can't just let you leave.

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:12.940
No one's more surprised than I am.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.730
Other people don't matter.

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:19.860
It's dumb to do something
for another person.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:23.820
Twelve years I've lived with that mindset.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:26.490
When I saw you suffering, Yuzu,

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:31.040
my body moved on its own,
intent on helping you.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:35.210
Before I knew it, I was doing
what I'd always mocked.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:43.390
Plus, if only I'd had medical knowledge,
I could have cured you myself.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:46.140
<i>That </i>was frustrating.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:47.890
Tamako-<i>san</i>...

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:52.690
Of course, someone from
the diabolical Shima family

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:56.940
might not be <i>able </i>to work
in the service of others.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.780
Still...

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:02.490
I want to be someone who helps people.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:08.740
Then, once I become a doctor,
I'll marry a nobleman

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:11.660
and have him build me my clinic!

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:13.500
And a villa, too!

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.750
Well? How's <i>that </i>for a plan?

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:29.100
Are you all packed?

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.100
Yes.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:37.060
There's a lot I wanted to tell you, but
I've narrowed it down to one thing.

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:38.230
What's that?

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:42.440
Uh... thanks.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.450
What?

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:47.320
Terrifying!

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:53.000
N-No, I mean... look, you
tended to Yuzu, right?

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:56.540
And I think your coming here,
to this house...

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:57.920
I'm glad you did.

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:04.470
You don't particularly have
any reason to thank me.

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:10.470
I just had a great idea!

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:14.060
Let's all sleep together tonight--
side by side!

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:16.100
--What? Me, too?!
--What? Tamahiko, too?!

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.860
Come to Kobe, won't you, sis?

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:24.110
I certainly will!

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:25.650
That's a promise!

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:34.870
♬ Do re mi fa so gently it blows ♬

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:41.170
♬ So la ti do: the bird
flutters into the sky ♬

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:42.050
Tamako...

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:43.630
♬ The scent of... ♬

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:45.760
I understand your anxiety.

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:49.840
Come t think of it,
out of all us siblings,

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.100
you and I were
two peas in a pod.

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:56.640
Always feeling that loneliness,

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:58.600
living with closed hearts...

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:04.440
How can I, as your brother,
ease your mind at times like this?

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.990
Peace of mind.

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:16.870
You'll be fine, Tamako.

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:18.790
You'll make one outstanding doctor.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:23.800
This is what I was missing--
this kind of compassion.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:29.930
If I'd known sooner, we could have
gotten along so well with each other.

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:35.560
You seem to think that I hate you...

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:38.560
...but that's just your assumption.

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:40.730
The family member I cherish the most

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:41.900
is you.

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:46.320
Wait--what am I doing?

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:51.990
"JNR"
"Sakura Station"

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:54.240
Tamako-<i>san</i>,

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:55.910
here's your lunch.

00:06:55.910 --> 00:07:00.500
Wow, all this for me? Thanks, Yuzu!

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.130
Please, be well...

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:04.290
C'mon, don't cry.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.760
Look! I'm Kotori-<i>chan</i>!

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:10.550
I'll be sure to write!

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:13.850
Oh, right: Tamahiko?

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:17.140
--You better treat Yuzu right or else!
--Here comes another scolding...

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:23.560
Next time, look me in the eye
when you pat my head.

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:26.480
It's hardly impressive
to do it while I'm asleep.

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:29.740
You were <i>awake</i>?!

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:32.030
The Ryogokubashi train is now leaving!

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:45.840
That look on my brother's face--too funny!

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:49.510
Oh, my!

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:52.430
"Good luck in your studies --Yuzuki"

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:52.430
Milk caramels--and almond macarons!

00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:57.680
"Human Anatomy"
"Read to stave off boredom --Your brother"

00:07:57.680 --> 00:07:59.680
"Read to stave off boredom."

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:04.900
Yuzu, my sister... Tamahiko, my brother...

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:09.150
Two important people
who've changed my life.

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:12.400
Thank you.

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:24.540
"September 1, Taisho 11 (1922)"
September already...

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:27.340
All right.

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:28.710
"General Mathematics"

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:32.880
It's not like I have any future prospects.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:36.390
For one thing, I'm dead
to the world at large,

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:40.430
so I hesitate to even
mention the word "future."

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:42.100
And yet...

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:46.020
I want to do what I can
now--whatever it may be.

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:48.940
After all, Tamako's out
there working hard.

00:08:51.650 --> 00:08:54.900
Waltzing on in again, eh?

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:56.280
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:01.540
I'm coming in.

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:04.710
I've brought you some tea.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.330
Ah, thanks.

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:11.300
Oh, Haru-<i>chan</i>. There you are.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:15.180
Since when did it have a name?

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:18.260
It'd be sad to be without one forever.

00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:19.720
Right, Haru-<i>chan</i>?

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:28.520
Oh, no! It's market day!

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:31.190
I'll head down to the village
for some shopping!

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:33.860
To the village?

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:37.110
That girl was bought, was she not?

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:41.030
Then to live deep in the
mountains with a <i>man</i>--alone.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:45.790
I'll be back!

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.130
Come on down!

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:51.750
Sweet <i>amazake </i>here!

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:57.470
Isn't that the girl from
the Shima boy's place?

00:09:57.470 --> 00:09:59.260
So that's her.

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:01.010
She's still so small...

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:07.060
I'd like some vegetables, please!

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:07.980
Sure thing!

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:09.940
What do you recommend today?

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:11.020
Let's see...

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:14.650
Hey, that's--

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:24.660
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>! But why?

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:31.840
I-I remembered that it was
about time for a... new book.

00:10:33.250 --> 00:10:37.220
Since... since I'm here,
I'll carry the basket.

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:38.050
Huh?

00:10:38.050 --> 00:10:42.220
You should really stock up...
make the most of it.

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:44.350
Or... that's what <i>I </i>think.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:48.140
You're right!

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:55.440
I knew it. They're gossiping
about Yuzu, too.

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:56.820
And it's all my fault.

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:05.580
How must she feel with all eyes on her?

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:12.170
What are you grinning about?

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:14.500
Huh? Was I grinning?

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:15.500
Mmm.

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:22.640
I was thinking I hadn't
shopped with you like this

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:25.260
since we went to Tokyo.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:27.100
It made me happy!

00:11:27.100 --> 00:11:28.980
R-Right...

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:51.500
What are you picking out?

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.830
Stationery for writing letters.

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:57.090
This one's for Tamako-<i>san</i>,
and this is for Midori-<i>san</i>.

00:11:57.090 --> 00:11:58.510
Midori-<i>san</i>?

00:11:58.510 --> 00:12:00.920
A friend from the girls' school.

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:05.140
They're selling books over there.

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:06.140
Eh?

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:09.970
Welcome!

00:12:11.270 --> 00:12:13.230
Have a look. Take your time!

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:16.020
I've been wanting to read this one!

00:12:16.020 --> 00:12:16.940
This, too!

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:19.980
Oh, wow... you even
have Tanizaki's latest!

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:24.490
You really like books,
don't you, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>.

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:27.080
Mmm-hmm.

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:32.540
My parents gave up
on me from an early age.

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:35.000
I always had a friend in books.

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:40.170
Father, today is September first.
Do you know what day--

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:46.140
Tamahiko, I don't need <i>you</i>
to tell <i>me </i>that it's September first!

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:48.720
I'm busy. Get out of here!

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:55.650
Nobody cares about me,

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:57.310
not one bit...

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:04.820
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:06.910
Oh--sorry.

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:10.040
I'll take this.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:11.790
That'll be 70 <i>sen</i>.

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:14.660
One, two... all set!

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:17.670
Say, if you like that one,
how about this here?

00:13:30.140 --> 00:13:33.480
Dinner's ready!

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:37.900
<i>Chirashi</i>, simmered fish, <i>hittsumi</i>...

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:39.860
It's like some kind of feast.

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:45.740
Well, it <i>is </i>your birthday, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:51.030
Huh?!

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:53.450
How... how did you...

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:58.040
It's only natural to know
<i>that </i>much if we're to be wed!

00:13:58.040 --> 00:13:59.960
Is that right...

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:04.630
Not really--I asked Tamako-<i>san</i>.

00:14:04.630 --> 00:14:09.180
And, well... I know it's not much, but...

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:12.140
This is my birthday present to you!

00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:15.390
It's...

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:19.020
A pressed-bellflower bookmark.

00:14:20.150 --> 00:14:23.900
It's not very well made, I'm afraid...

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:29.030
I thought it would be good for you,
since you like to read.

00:14:29.030 --> 00:14:35.160
And I've always thought
bellflowers suited you.

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:42.920
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:46.170
Um... right.

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:49.800
Sorry. This is... this is a first.

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:53.680
Now my hand's shaking...

00:15:01.190 --> 00:15:04.020
Happy birthday!

00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:10.740
All alone again this year...

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:15.990
It's my birthday, and nobody... nobody...

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:49.900
Ta-Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:51.610
"Happy birthday."

00:15:51.610 --> 00:15:55.280
Hearing those words
for the very first time,

00:15:55.280 --> 00:16:00.210
it felt as though even my
past self found salvation.

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:01.210
Thank you...

00:16:04.170 --> 00:16:07.710
My treasure--always and forever.

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:14.970
Ta--

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:20.680
Th-Th-This bookmark, that is!

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:22.440
Oh... aha!

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:32.490
What was that?

00:16:32.490 --> 00:16:34.410
Maybe Haru-<i>chan</i>?

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:36.780
Not that cat again...

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:38.030
I'll go chase it out.

00:16:50.210 --> 00:16:53.590
What have I <i>done</i>?!

00:16:53.590 --> 00:16:57.100
Now Yuzu's going to think
I'm some kind of weirdo...

00:16:57.100 --> 00:17:00.770
She probably thinks that already!

00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:02.310
Still...

00:17:02.310 --> 00:17:05.770
I've never gotten a
birthday present before.

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:12.320
Just as I suspected--in my room.

00:17:13.030 --> 00:17:15.610
Sneaking in again...

00:17:15.610 --> 00:17:17.160
Enough of your mischief--

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:29.460
Huh?!

00:17:36.590 --> 00:17:38.680
Who...

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:39.850
Who are you?

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:44.180
What are you doing in my room?

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:57.110
Pleasure.

00:17:57.110 --> 00:18:00.410
I live down in the village.

00:18:00.410 --> 00:18:02.330
Pleased to meet you.

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:03.330
Huh?

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:09.330
Her leisurely attitude,
without a hint of panic...

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:11.750
What's her deal?

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:14.210
Oh, man... spooky!

00:18:15.130 --> 00:18:18.550
Come on--don't brace yourself like that.

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:21.810
I only came by to say hello.

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:24.970
By the way, rich boy...

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:26.730
"Juicy Night-Time Club - Special Edition"

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:26.730
By the way, rich boy...

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:29.520
"Juicy Night-Time Club - Special Edition"

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:29.520
You read some <i>amazing </i>stuff!

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:34.360
You have every issue
that's ever been published!

00:18:35.490 --> 00:18:37.780
Don't look at those!

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:41.620
And <i>this </i>is the famous Shima family son!

00:18:43.540 --> 00:18:47.080
Men really are hopeless!

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:51.420
If you happen to be interested
in that kind of thing...

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:54.380
...you could always do it with me.

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:55.380
Huh?!

00:18:58.050 --> 00:18:59.590
She smells good...

00:19:07.310 --> 00:19:10.560
<i>Obviously </i>I was lying!
Did you think I was serious?!

00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:11.730
I did <i>not</i>!

00:19:14.270 --> 00:19:16.400
Oh, that was fun!

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:20.530
Well, I'm all set here,
so I'll just head back.

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:22.320
What? Wait!

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:25.700
What are you going to do
about the jar of caramels?

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:28.620
Caramels? Oh, right.

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:31.620
They're too sweet and stick
to my teeth. No, thanks.

00:19:31.620 --> 00:19:34.920
No one was offering!

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:37.590
I'm asking about the broken ja--

00:19:40.180 --> 00:19:41.340
She's <i>fast</i>!

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:44.970
Later!

00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:49.600
What just happened?

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:52.100
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:53.100
Coming...

00:19:55.230 --> 00:19:58.650
Was Haru-<i>chan </i>all right?

00:19:58.650 --> 00:20:03.450
Huh? Oh--yeah.
I just chased the cat outside.

00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:06.370
But the caramel jar was a casualty.

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:08.160
Oh, dear...

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:10.750
You're not hurt, are you?

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:13.580
I wonder if Haru-<i>chan</i>'s okay...

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:16.290
I-I don't think you have to worry!

00:20:16.290 --> 00:20:17.710
Listen, Yuzu!

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:20.670
Thank you again for the bookmark!

00:20:20.670 --> 00:20:23.180
I'm going to start using it right away!

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:25.390
Now, which book should I use it in?

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:31.480
I'm so glad you like it!

00:20:33.060 --> 00:20:35.310
I just <i>had </i>to go for a cover-up...

00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:40.320
Huh?

00:20:44.320 --> 00:20:45.320
It's gone!

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:49.240
Don't tell me...

00:20:54.250 --> 00:20:57.040
Where are you going, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:58.380
I'll be right back!

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:09.350
Only that... that's all!

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:16.100
She can have my wallet,
but not that bookmark!

00:21:18.570 --> 00:21:22.280
That gift came straight from Yuzu's heart!

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:32.830
Smells like... a woman...

00:21:38.290 --> 00:21:41.000
Boy, <i>that </i>was a cinch!

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:45.050
The little rich boy needs
to watch his pockets!

00:21:45.050 --> 00:21:48.180
He never even noticed
that I nicked his wallet.

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:51.720
A bookmark?

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:56.270
Was it his? Wonder what flower that is...

00:21:56.270 --> 00:21:59.980
Well, whatever! I'll hang onto this, too.

00:23:38.410 --> 00:23:42.750
I'm glad we were able to celebrate
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>'s birthday.

00:23:42.750 --> 00:23:47.800
He seems to like the
pressed-bellflower bookmark, too.

00:23:47.800 --> 00:23:53.220
But... he <i>has </i>been
acting a little strange...
